On-device AI refers to AI (Artificial Intelligence) systems that run locally on a device, like a smartphone or computer, without requiring the device to connect to a cloud server. This means the AI models are trained using data from the device itself, not external sources. This approach improves privacy and data security, as the AI doesn’t rely on external servers. Examples include voice assistants, smart home devices, and facial recognition apps. It’s about real-time use and local data handling.

